{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report (local repair complete; not pushed or closed).\n\nProblem: `attach_commits` rejected valid code commits when `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` relocated ticket storage outside the code checkout.\n\nProven root cause: `_lib_mutations.attach_commits` passed the tracker path into `commit_impact.unresolvable_shas`; `code_root_for` then used `dirname(tracker)` as the code repository. Runtime tracing observed `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse`, so a valid code SHA was looked up in the wrong repository (`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:255,269`; former `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py:135-147`).\n\nProof: the same real `HEAD` returned resolvable at the code root and unresolvable at the relocated tracker parent. Passing explicit `repo_root=<code-root>` still failed and traced the tracker parent, rejecting the CLI-omission rival. Changing only the validation root made the valid attachment persist while a bogus SHA remained rejected. Default nested tracker behavior succeeded.\n\nTest: `tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py::test_attach_resolves_code_repo_independently_from_relocated_tracker` uses a real Git checkout and independently moved real tracker. It proves the dangerous preconditions, exact attachment receipt/persisted COMMITS state, and mixed valid/invalid all-or-nothing state. It was collected and observed RED before repair at the valid-commit call, GREEN after repair, then RED again under the exact `tracker.parent` mutation; restoration returned GREEN. The final-form raw-regex lint adjustment was also re-proven RED under the mutation before the fix was restored. The oracle asserts public return/persisted state, so behavior-preserving internal refactors do not break it.\n\nFix: validate the whole batch with `commit_impact.invalid_commit_shas(..., str(config.repo_root(repo_root)))`, preserving tracker lookup/append through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`. Delete `code_root_for` and `unresolvable_shas`, whose only production reference was this call chain, so the invalid tracker-derived prior art cannot be reused.\n\nScope and safety: CLI (`_commands/attach_commits.py:28`), MCP (`_mcp_writes.py:89-97`), and public library all converge on `_lib_mutations.attach_commits`; no caller depends on tracker-parent validation. This restores the documented relocated-store contract, adds no dependency or capability, preserves all-or-nothing state, and weakens no existing test. Repository search finds no remaining production `code_root_for` or `unresolvable_shas`.\n\nSiblings/parity: construct sweep covered the exact commit-validation helper/call family; no additional `invalid_commit_shas` caller derives code root from tracker storage. The previously confirmed close-precheck sibling was already repaired by parent `tekite-fleece-hake`/merged commit `548e4d2997`. Parity rule: attach-commits SHA validation must use the code repository independently of tracker storage. CLI, MCP, and library all hold through the shared seam; automated caller is N/A (none); the close-side consumer does not validate newly attached input and its analogous code-root defect is the merged parent fix. No parity slot is missing.\n\nVerification: focused attach/store selection 31 passed; full `tests/interfaces/store` reached 433 passed, 9 skipped, with one deterministic unrelated current-main failure in `test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout` (`ModuleNotFoundError: rebar_reconciler`). `make lint` passed, `make typecheck` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. The unrelated failure reproduces alone and is filed as `fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle` (79c6-eaf3-38af-4ce9), linked discovered_from this bug.\n\nResidual risk/prevention: the only observed residual is that pre-existing reconciler import failure; disposition: ticket filed as `fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle`. No residual fragility observed in the attach-commits repair.\n\nReplication: the original disposable CLI scenario now prints `commits attached ...: 1` with the external tracker and persists exactly `commits: [{sha: HEAD}]`; a subsequent `HEAD definitely-not-a-commit` batch still errors `nothing was recorded` and leaves the single existing attachment unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787045535631540001,"uuid":"ea07e14d-4fdf-4b93-8ec9-cad92eceeb0b"}